{
  "id": "s04-l04",
  "unit": "s04-conjuncts",
  "title": "Conjuncts 4: ফলা signs and রেফ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**ফলা** (fola) are small forms of য, র, ব that attach to a consonant.\n\n**য-ফলা ্য** is a little flag on the right. In the middle of a word it **doubles** the consonant: ধন্যবাদ = `dhonnobad`, সন্ধ্যা = `shondha`. With া it often makes an *æ* sound: হ্যাঁ (`hya~`, *yes*), ব্যাগ (`bæg`).\n\n**র-ফলা ্র** is a slanted stroke under the letter and adds an r: ছাত্র (`chhatro`), গ্রাম (`gram`, *village*), প্রতিদিন (`protidin`, *every day*). **রেফ র্** is the opposite: a small hook *on top* that means an r **before** the letter: দুর্গাপূজা (`durgapuja`), পর্যন্ত (`porjonto`).\n\n**ব-ফলা ্ব** is usually **silent**: স্বামী (`shami`, *husband*), স্বাধীনতা (`shadhinota`, *independence*). In the middle of a word it doubles the consonant instead.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "cj-jofola",
      "bn": "ন্য",
      "tr": "nno",
      "en": "্য (jo-fola) on ন: doubles the n (ধন্যবাদ)",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ্য (U+09CD U+09AF), name jo-fola (য-ফলা). ন্য = ন + ্ + য. Mid-word it doubles the consonant; with া at the start it gives æ (ব্যাগ bæg). Sounds like ন্ন: keep apart in listening tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-rofola",
      "bn": "ত্র",
      "tr": "tro",
      "en": "্র (ro-fola) on ত: t + r (ছাত্র)",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ্র (U+09CD U+09B0), name ro-fola (র-ফলা), a slanted stroke under the letter. ত্র = ত + ্ + র."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-bofola",
      "bn": "স্ব",
      "tr": "sho",
      "en": "্ব (bo-fola) on স: the ব is silent (স্বামী = shami)",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ্ব (U+09CD U+09AC), name bo-fola (ব-ফলা). At the start of a word it is silent; in the middle it doubles the consonant (বিশ্ব bishsho). স্ব = স + ্ + ব."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-ref",
      "bn": "র্গ",
      "tr": "rgo",
      "en": "র্ (ref): an r before the consonant, drawn as a hook on top",
      "notes": "Name: ref (রেফ), র + ্ written as a small hook above the next consonant. র্গ = র U+09B0 + ্ + গ U+0997 (দুর্গা durga)."
    }
  ],
